      "imageAt": [
        0,
        0.4
      ],
      "seconds": 21.24,
      "text": "We did not discover dark matter and dark energy. We named them. They are placeholders, the shape of a hole in the accounts, labeled so we can keep working. It is the same move astronomers once made when Mercury's orbit refused to behave, and the answer turned out to be that gravity itself needed rewriting. So the honest version is this. The largest thing in physics right now is a gap.",
